{"name":"What We Do in the Shadows","hex":"#441122","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"what","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["Which, especially which of an open-ended set of possibilities.","Which."]},{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["Which thing, event, circumstance, etc.: used in asking for the specification of an identity, quantity, quality, etc.","That which; those that; the thing(s) that."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/what"},{"term":"shadows","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shadow"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shadow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadows"}],"entries":[{"title":"What We Do in the Shadows","blocks":[{"text":"What We Do in the Shadows is a 2014 New Zealand mockumentary comedy horror film written and directed by Jemaine Clement and Taika Waititi and the first installment in the What We Do in the Shadows franchise. The film also stars Clement and Waititi, along with Jonathan Brugh, Ben Fransham, Cori Gonzalez-Macuer, Stu Rutherford, and Jackie van Beek. The film's plot concerns several vampires who live together in a flat in Wellington."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/70/What_We_Do_in_the_Shadows_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_We_Do_in_the_Shadows"},{"title":"What We Do in the Shadows (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"What We Do in the Shadows is an American comedy horror mockumentary fantasy television series created by Jemaine Clement, first broadcast on FX on March 27, 2019, until concluding its run with the end of its sixth season on December 16, 2024. Based on the 2014 New Zealand film written and directed by Clement and Taika Waititi, both of whom act as executive producers, the series follows four vampire roommates on Staten Island, and stars Kayvan Novak, Matt Berry, Natasia Demetriou, Harvey Guillén, Mark Proksch, and Kristen Schaal."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/31/What_We_Do_in_the_Shadows_Title_Card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_We_Do_in_the_Shadows_(TV_series)"},{"title":"What We Do","blocks":[{"text":"What We Do is a studio album by jazz guitarist John Scofield, the second to be released as the John Scofield Quartet. It was recorded in May 1992 and released the following year on Blue Note. The quartet features saxophonist Joe Lovano, bassist Dennis Irwin and drummer Bill Stewart. Irwin had previously recorded with Scofield on the Bennie Wallace album Sweeping Through the City, and went on to play on two additional Scofield albums: Hand Jive (1994) and Groove Elation (1995)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/70/John_Scofield_What_We_Do.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/What_We_Do"},{"title":"We","blocks":[{"text":"In Modern English, we is a plural, first-person pronoun."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/We"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Fuenf_Zimmer_Kueche_Sarg_What_We_Do_In_The_Shadows_Movie_Opening_Berlin_2014_Jemaine_Clement_Taika_Waititi_Mark_Benecke_Vampire_Movie.jpg/500px-Fuenf_Zimmer_Kueche_Sarg_What_We_Do_In_The_Shadows_Movie_Opening_Berlin_2014_Jemaine_Clement_Taika_Waititi_Mark_Benecke_Vampire_Movie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Fuenf_Zimmer_Kueche_Sarg_What_We_Do_In_The_Shadows_Movie_Opening_Berlin_2014_Jemaine_Clement_Taika_Waititi_Mark_Benecke_Vampire_Movie.jpg/1280px-Fuenf_Zimmer_Kueche_Sarg_What_We_Do_In_The_Shadows_Movie_Opening_Berlin_2014_Jemaine_Clement_Taika_Waititi_Mark_Benecke_Vampire_Movie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped